(RESERVE BANK OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(Digital Lending Guidelines 2022) Tj
T*
(RBI/2022-23/111 DOR.CRE.REC.66/21.07.001/2022-23) Tj
T*
(Issued: September 2, 2022) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(GUIDELINES ON DIGITAL LENDING) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(These guidelines apply to all Regulated Entities \(REs\) including Non-Banking Financial) Tj
T*
(Companies \(NBFCs\) and their Lending Service Providers \(LSPs\) engaged in digital lending.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(=============================================================================) Tj
T*
(SECTION A: KEY FACT STATEMENT \(KFS\) REQUIREMENTS) Tj
T*
(=============================================================================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Clause 2.1 - Key Fact Statement Mandatory Disclosure) Tj
T*
(All digital loans must be accompanied by a Key Fact Statement \(KFS\) that discloses) Tj
T*
(all material terms of the loan in a standardised format prescribed by RBI.) Tj
T*
(The KFS must be provided to the borrower prior to execution of the loan agreement.) Tj
T*
(No digital loan shall be disbursed without receipt of signed KFS from the borrower.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Clause 2.2 - Annual Percentage Rate \(APR\)) Tj
T*
(The Annual Percentage Rate \(APR\) must be explicitly and prominently stated in the KFS.) Tj
T*
(The APR must be inclusive of ALL upfront charges, processing fees, insurance premiums,) Tj
T*
(documentation charges, verification fees and any other fee levied on the borrower.) Tj
T*
(The APR shall be expressed as an annualised rate so borrowers can compare loan products.) Tj
T*
(Non-disclosure of APR, partial disclosure, or disclosure that excludes any fee or charge) Tj
T*
(constitutes a direct violation of these guidelines \(Page 4, Clause 2.2\).) Tj
T*
(Regulated Entities must ensure the APR calculation methodology is transparent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Clause 2.3 - Penal Charges) Tj
T*
(Penal charges for default or delayed repayment must be disclosed in the KFS as a FLAT FEE.) Tj
T*
(Penal charges shall NOT be in the nature of penal interest that compounds over time.) Tj
T*
(Compounding of penal charges on the outstanding principal or interest is strictly prohibited.) Tj
T*
(The quantum of penal charges must be reasonable, proportionate and disclosed upfront.) Tj
T*
(Any NBFC levying compounded penal interest instead of a flat penal charge shall be in) Tj
T*
(violation of these Digital Lending Guidelines \(Page 5, Clause 2.3\).) Tj
T*
(Penal charges must be expressed as a specific rupee amount \(e.g., Rs. 500 per month of) Tj
T*
(delay\) and NOT as a percentage that accrues or compounds on the outstanding amount.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Clause 2.4 - Cooling-Off Period / Look-Up Period) Tj
T*
(Every digital loan product must provide a cooling-off period \(also called look-up period\).) Tj
T*
(The minimum cooling-off period for digital loans is THREE \(3\) days for loan tenors above) Tj
T*
(seven days and ONE \(1\) day for loan tenors equal to or below seven days.) Tj
T*
(During the cooling-off period, the borrower may exit the loan by repaying only the) Tj
T*
(principal and proportionate APR without being subject to any prepayment penalty.) Tj
T*
(The Key Fact Statement must explicitly state the cooling-off period in number of days.) Tj
T*
(Failure to provide the minimum prescribed cooling-off period, or failure to mention it in) Tj
T*
(the KFS, constitutes a violation of RBI Digital Lending Guidelines \(Page 5, Clause 2.4\).) Tj
T*
(LSPs and NBFCs must honour exit requests made within the cooling-off window.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Clause 2.5 - Grievance Redressal Officer) Tj
T*
(The Key Fact Statement must explicitly state the name and complete contact details of) Tj
T*
(the Nodal Grievance Redressal Officer designated by the NBFC.) Tj
T*
(Contact details must include: full name, email address, phone number, and postal address.) Tj
T*
(The Nodal Grievance Officer must be accessible to borrowers for all complaints related) Tj
T*
ET

